      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-02-06_WidnesExaminer_art0025" n="art0025">
        <head>NEW GAME.</head>
        <p>THE NEW GAME.</p>
        <p>One of the natural outcomes of the present po;ltical situation is a new game, which has been christened " Fiscalitis," after Mr. Asquith's now popular phrase. This game enters into the spirit of the day, and is on the most approved political lines. The pieces on the board are ,ike those used in Halma, but the system of the game is more like draughts. It is played by two people, one being a Free Trader, and having four white pieces, which are called after the Duke of Devonshire, the Earl of Rosebery, Sir Henry Campbell-Bannerman, and Mr. Asquith. The other is a Protectionist and has eight black pieces, under the leadership of Mr. Chamber- lain. The board is inside a bait, and is</p>
        <p>_ - -- ---, ~........_ - r --------=-----e&amp;www----_,-...-.. \ 1 .....-_, -,.: ....:::::!2.,,v'.•:.,-./..:27.„ ----- . :i" --,'-2::,-0111.1111.1111._ •;,,, ', . = ' ;', .! '-',;,1,-,1 i ~.‘1... --J- ..•111,g -1.11._,11 ,z i.' ' ,',. , • 'it, 02'..t ' .....4 ' ..... •1 : : ' •-.-.1 ' * .4=P, .. '' ' , E__ • s..- •::::; , , "'-_" - - -I'. ''',r'.' ••• '..,il:•' '1'.;...,' i"."-..-.-- , ~; ~.....__ ~,,,;, ' - t.s.,'„'• Aminig [ .4-' 'oo??zMin'''‘iiq't,' • ..,\::t,.,-t_tiP, r"''''--,</p>
