      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-02-06_WidnesExaminer_art0043" n="art0043">
        <head>WEAR AND TEAR OF CITY LIFE.</head>
        <p>THE WEAR AND TEAR OF CITY LIFE.</p>
        <p>Why do so many of our City men look so sickly? Because they drink too much tea, and when they are fagged out cannot take more substantial and nutritive food. ,The system thus fgradually becomes weakened and debilitated:: there is no relish for food, ho energy for work, and the whole of the physical:and mental con- dition becomes seriously deranged. One City clerk—Mr. H. W. Elliott, 23, Norfolk-road, Canonbury, N.—writes : "I work late hours, Ibut I find Dr. Tibbles' Vi-Cocoa a delicious and stimulating drink. My doctor, grocer, and, chemist speak very highly of it." And if you use Vi-Cocoa regularly you will speak very highly of it too. Sold in 6d. packets and 9d. and is. 6d. tins everywhere.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-02-06_WidnesExaminer_art0044" n="art0044">
        <head>Warrington Ragged School and Mission.</head>
        <p>Warrington Ragged School and Mission.</p>
        <p>On Wednesday evening, a tea party was given to over four hundred of the poor children of the town by Mr. R. A. and Miss Naylor in the above School. The wants of the little ones were attended to by Messrs. Skelland, Parton, Crozier and Odell, and Misses Monk, Titchard, Leadbetter and Barlow. After the tea a capital limelight entertainment was held when about a hundred slides were thrown on the sheet, consist- ing of local views and comic slides under the direction of Mr. F. J. Owen, which the children greatly enjoyed The lantern was manipulated by Mr. Owen jun., and Mr. W. Wright. At the close a hearty vote of thanks was 4ccorded amid applause to Mr. and Miss Naylor for their kindness in providing the tea. Upon leav- ing each child received an orange. It is the intention of the committee to give more of these teas if the generously-disposed will kindly send the suitable means and will also either give or lend some lantern slides.</p>
      </div>
