        <p>directors were determined to push the matter to a com- pletion as rapidly as possible. The report was adopted. "Alderman H. S. Timmis was re-elected a director, and Mr. Frank Gaskell was elected a director in place of BRUT IL ATTACK ON A CONSTABLE. Alderman Wareing, who retired and was thanked for At the Town Hall, on Monday, Edward and 'John his past services. Leahey, brokers, of Smithy-brow, were charged with a On the proposition of Mr. Neilson, seconded by Mr. breach of the neaceand with assaulting Police-constable W. Hindley, Mr. Benjamin Cookson was re-appointed Barker. The officer gave evidence that the prisoners joint auditor. Mr. Handley said he had been asked were creating a disturbance on Saturday, and when he that if it took ten days to get the third cable across, spoke to them they turned upon him and committeda how long would it take to carry thirty-eight cables violent assault.-4 They were joined by another man over. (Laughter.) The opening date had been pre- named Riley, who had got away, and the three men dieted as June, 1905. kicked him savagely about the legs, struck him with The Chairman said Mr. Handley might tell his friends their fists on tre face, and badly tore his uniform. that none of them were content with a 3 per cent. divi- Assistance arrived and the two Leaheys were secured. dend. They all expected a good deal more, and the Chief Constable Wood reported that both men had been sooner the bridge was got to work the sooner the share- convicted on over forty occasions for assaults on the holders would have a return. After all,those who found police and other offences. The bench committed both the mork y expected some gratitude. (Laughter. men to prison, Edward for six months and John for A vote of thanks concluded the proceedings. three months, with hard labour in each case.</p>
