        <p>this report he was prepared to move that the Water Engineer be given three months notice determining his office. The MAYOR: You cannot do that. Alderman PIERPOLNT said that alter this long dis- cussionhe hoped the Chairman of the Water Commit- tee would be consistent and move that the report be not adopted. Alderman FRANCOMB : Not at all. Alderman PIERPOINT : You have objected to it all along. Alderman FRANCOMB said they agreed with every word of the report. He was exceedingly sorry that they had got men who would allow such things. He had not the slightest idea that the Special Committee would have liked to be present at the interview or he would have invited them. He only desired to serve the best interests of the ratepayers. Councillor Pemberton did more than anyone else at the committee meeting. He himself did not askone leading question of the men. The subject then dropped on the understanding that the report would receive the attention of the Water Committee.</p>
