        <p>'MADE 1..1 G-'l, • RESULTS OF' SATURDAY'S MATCHES. - • LIAI, , STOCKTON HEATH V. SOUTH MANCHESTER. ROYAL - At Stockton Heath. Both teams were at full strength. . - BICYCLES - From the bully off South pressed, and with a fine run . • 'O,O on the left by Whitehead, who shot at goal and hit the goal corner. Parson " Allen following up scored the• ENFIELD MOTORS first goal. Even play followed until half-time, South leading by one goal to nil. Give-and-take play followed. From a scrummage near the circle, and good Sicycics Ms. to £.16 16s. Motor B,tycl. - 4.3 and 41:: GtOneas following up, Stockton Heath scored by the aid of ' ra.ter . C.t75 .ar,t .C 303. Richardson. There was no further score and the game ended in a draw of one goal each. . WARRINGTON ROYAL v. TIMPERLEY " B." At Timperley, on a heavy ground. The visitors scored in the first minute through Hatton and shortly afterwards Whittle added a second. The home team rallied, and the opposing backs had to defend. Bailey kicked lout two or three times. The Warringtonians then got back to the Timperley quarters, and Skelton scored just before half-time; the homesters made a futile attempt to break through. In the second moiety Timperley netted the ball with a fast shot, and Skelton scored again for the visitors. Result :—Warrington Royal, four goals; Timperley "B," one goal.</p>
